{%- comment -%}
  Petsome Ld: inline icon.

  The "Ld" sections force the body font on every descendant
  (`#section-id * { font-family: ... }`), and that selector outranks the
  `.material-symbols-outlined` rule Google Fonts ships - which would replace the
  icon font with the body font and leave the raw ligature text on screen
  ("verified_user" clipped to "ve"). These are the same Material Symbols glyphs
  as real paths instead, so they cannot be broken by a font rule and need no
  webfont to load.

  Usage: {% render 'petsome-ld-icon', icon: 'star' %}

  The svg is sized in `em`, so set `font-size` on it (or its parent) to scale it,
  and `color` to recolour it - exactly like the icon font behaved.
{%- endcomment -%}
